course: dictionary
lesson: 10445
title: Trump: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. Trump is a good example. Look for clues first: cards, a game, a name, a sound.
explain: To trump something means to beat it by doing something better. If Ana tells a story and Ben tells a better one, Ben has trumped her story. The clue is "better", so trump must mean beat.
explain: Trump is also a name. «Mr Trump, president before from 2017 to 2021» has a capital letter, a title and dates, so Trump is a person's family name here, not a card. Capital letters and titles are clues too.
fact: A trump is a suit of cards that beats all the others in a game.
fact: In Top Trumps, a trump card wins the round.
fact: «Trump» as a verb means to beat something by doing it better, as in «she trumped his story».
fact: Your trump card is your best secret advantage, the thing you save for when you need it.
fact: Trump is also a family name: Donald Trump is an American businessman who became President of the United States.
exercise: Sam says, «Your story was great, but mine trumped it.» What does trumped mean? | Forgot it | Read it aloud | Copied it exactly | *Beat it by being better
exercise: In a card game, what is a trump? | A card that has been torn | A card with no picture | A card you must give away | *A suit of cards that beats all the others
exercise: Which sentence uses Trump as a name? | «Her trump card was a secret.» | «The last trump sounds at the end of time.» | «She trumped his story by telling a funnier one.» | *«Mr Trump was president from 2017 to 2021.»
test: In «Your trump card is your best secret advantage», what does trump card mean? | Something you give away on purpose | A card that loses the game | A card from an old game | *Your best secret advantage
test: «News reports said Joe Biden won the 2020 election with 306 electors to Donald Trump's 232.» Here Trump is a | A trumpet | *Family name of a person | A type of car | A card in a game
exam: In the Bible, «the last trump» means the last | secret advantage | name of a president | playing card | *trumpet sound
